:"another option came about while chatting with @satra \n- [ ] implement an option to register a dataset within cache (as a remote; upon install or after) so it could fetch/annex merge dataset's git-annex branch, and thus to enrich its knowledge about (global) availability of the keys.\n\nThis would require access and permissions to work on the cache.\nIn some way then the cache  could serve as an alternative to the UltimateDB (#436).\nWould need to be first checked on the subject of scalability (I will now try to quickly make such a dataset from all the datasets we have for datasets.datalad.org and see how it goes)\n\nedit1: so I have ran a script which annex merged (incrementally) all datasets we have atm available from datasets.datalad.org (made it into 528 remotes ;-) not all are annexes).  Took around 5 hours and by the end each annex merge was taking around 1-2 minutes, here is the end trail of the log where I also did the final `git annex merge` just in case\n```\n+ /mnt/btrfs/datasets/datalad/crawl/workshops/repronim-sfn-2017/challenge\n    merging workshops--repronim-sfn-2017--challenge elapsed=1:07.94 objects=3418m #files=2453629\nI: merging all elapsed=0:00.24 objects=3418m #files=2453629\nI: gc elapsed=18:05.49 objects=1775m #files=2453629\nI: final elapsed=0:00.00 objects=1775m #files=2453629\n```\nSo there is ~2.4M keys indexed, which takes 1.8GB of .git/objects space... Sounds like a bit too much.  Also now any query like `git annex whereis` is not that speedy -- about 2-3 sec:\n```\ngit)smaug:~datalad/datalad-ultimate-cache/full1[master]git\n$\u003e time git annex whereis --key MD5E-s5663237--4608ffbd6b78ce3a325eb338fa556589.nii.gz\nwhereis MD5E-s5663237--4608ffbd6b78ce3a325eb338fa556589.nii.gz (4 copies) \n        00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001 -- web\n        899f0347-0888-48ef-91b6-bac213ca8cef -- datalad-archives\n        c8bd3d05-33d4-4b59-9d53-ca7efbdcdd13 -- yoh@smaug:/mnt/btrfs/datasets/datalad/crawl/openfmri/ds000001 [openfmri--ds00000